This is a textbook "coverage theater" suite. Every production method is called (→ 95% coverage), but almost nothing is actually **verified**. Here's the severity-ranked audit:

---

## 🔴 Critical — No Assertion At All (tests prove nothing)

### 1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)
Calls `AddProduct` but never checks it was persisted.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var result = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(result);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", result.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, result.Price);
```

### 2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)
Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

### 3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)
Calls `RemoveProduct` but never checks the product is gone.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

### 4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)
Captures no return value; asserts nothing. Count could return -1 and this passes.
```csharp
// Fix:
Assert.AreEqual(0, _catalog.GetProductCount());
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

### 5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)
Applies a 10% discount but never checks any price was reduced. A bug in the discount formula (e.g. `Price * fraction` instead of `Price * (1 - fraction)`) would pass.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

### 6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84)
Imports a CSV line but never checks a product was created.
```csharp
// Fix:
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var product = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(product);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", product.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, product.Price);
```

---

## 🟠 High — Weak/Meaningless Assertion

### 7. `GetProduct_Works` (line 22)
Asserts `IsNotNull` only — doesn't verify the returned product has the right SKU, name, or price. A store returning *any* non-null object would pass.
```csharp
